   "widgets_values": [
    "{\"version\": 1, \"content\": \"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"model-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Models to download</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Orange. Each one needs a file from the list in the note above.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Diffusion Model (Qwen Image 2.1)</b> - The image model itself, 7B, from Alibaba's Qwen team.</li><li><b>Load CLIP (Qwen3-VL 8B)</b> - Reads your prompt and looks at your pictures.</li><li><b>Load VAE</b> - Turns pictures into the model's own format and back. It works with four channels, red, green, blue and transparency, which is how this model can hand back a transparent picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The numbers you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you have to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>1. Load Image</b> - The person. Here a man in a head-and-shoulders photo. In the prompt it is <code>&lt;image1&gt;</code>.</li><li><b>2. Load Image</b> - An object for the person to hold. Here the black mug with the Pixaroma logo. In the prompt it is <code>&lt;image2&gt;</code>.</li><li><b>3. Load Image</b> - The place. Here a room with a wicker armchair and nobody in it. In the prompt it is <code>&lt;image3&gt;</code>.</li><li><b>4. Pick Orientation and Size</b> - The size and shape of the new picture, any shape you like: it does not follow the pictures. The starred sizes are Qwen's native 2K ones and much slower.</li><li><b>5. Add a prompt</b> - What to make, and what to keep. Name the pictures by their tags.</li><li><b>6. Seed Random/Fixed?</b> - Fixed repeats the same result, Random rolls a new one each Run.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The speed nodes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Teal, above the graph.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Qwen Image 2.1 Cache</b> - Where the model keeps what it has already worked out about your pictures and the prompt, so it does not redo that on every step. Leave it on <b>auto</b> / <b>default</b>. The note in <b>workflow 1 (Outfit Change)</b> says when to change it.</li><li><b>Model Attention Backend</b> - Set to <b>comfy kitchen attention</b>, a faster way to do the model's attention maths. It changes the speed, not the picture. On a graphics card that cannot use it, ComfyUI falls back to normal attention by itself.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The render</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. These run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Text Encode Qwen Image 2.1</b> - Reads your prompt and your pictures, and resizes the pictures to about 1024 x 1024 first.  Its negative prompt box does nothing at CFG 1, the setting this model is made for, so leave it empty.</li><li><b>Empty Latent Image</b> - The blank canvas, at the size from step 4. The encoder's own canvas would copy picture 1's shape.</li><li><b>KSampler</b> - The render: 25 steps, euler, simple, CFG 1, the settings from ComfyUI's own template.</li><li><b>VAE Decode</b> - Turns the finished render into a picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Preview Image Pixaroma</b> - Shows the result and saves it to your output folder as a PNG.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p>There is no Compare node here: the result is a new picture made from all of yours, so there is no single before picture to hold it against. The dark <b>Run Timer</b> above it shows how long the last Run took.</p>\", \"buttonColor\": \"#f66744\", \"lineColor\": \"#f66744\", \"width\": 720, \"height\": 1082, \"backgroundColor\": \"#2a2a2a\"}",
    ""
   ],
