   "widgets_values": [
    "{\"version\": 1, \"content\": \"<h1>SETTINGS AND RUN TIME</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;What this workflow makes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>One new photo from all three pictures: the man from picture 1 sitting in the room from picture 3, holding the mug from picture 2.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Every number below was measured on a <b>24 GB RTX 4090</b> with this workflow and its own settings, each run on a fresh seed with the models already loaded. A different card gives different numbers, but the shape holds: the cost goes up with the pixels.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How long a Run takes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>What changed</th><th>1024 x 1024</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New pictures or prompt</td><td>14 s</td></tr><tr><td>New seed only</td><td>11 s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>For bigger sizes, see the table in <b>workflow 1 (Outfit Change)</b>: native 2K took about five times as long as 1 MP there, and it grows the same way here.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The graphics card peaked at about <b>19 GB</b> during these runs.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Writing the prompt</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Name each picture by its tag, <code>&lt;image1&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;image3&gt;</code>, and say what the person does with the object and where.</li><li>People and objects on a plain background are the easiest for the model to take from.</li><li><b>Say what must not change.</b> <code>Keep the room from &lt;image3&gt; exactly the same</code> keeps the whole room, so he sits in it at its own scale. For a closer photo, say how close the shot is instead, like <code>a medium shot from the waist up</code>.</li><li>Pick the shape of the new picture in step 4. To keep the room as it is, pick the room picture's shape: the demo room is square, so 1024 x 1024.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Tested on 8 seeds: every one kept his face, beard and black t-shirt, sat him in the wicker chair holding the mug with the logo to the camera, and kept the room. On 5 of them the room lines up with the room picture to within 2 pixels; on the other 3 the view moved a little.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The other edit workflows</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Kitchen attention, the memory node, the first Run of the session and the full size table are explained in <b>workflow 1 (Outfit Change)</b>. They work the same way here.</p>\", \"buttonColor\": \"#f66744\", \"lineColor\": \"#f66744\", \"width\": 810, \"height\": 767, \"backgroundColor\": \"#2a2a2a\"}",
    ""
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "note_json": "{\"version\": 1, \"content\": \"<h1>SETTINGS AND RUN TIME</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;What this workflow makes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>One new photo from all three pictures: the man from picture 1 sitting in the room from picture 3, holding the mug from picture 2.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Every number below was measured on a <b>24 GB RTX 4090</b> with this workflow and its own settings, each run on a fresh seed with the models already loaded. A different card gives different numbers, but the shape holds: the cost goes up with the pixels.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How long a Run takes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>What changed</th><th>1024 x 1024</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New pictures or prompt</td><td>14 s</td></tr><tr><td>New seed only</td><td>11 s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>For bigger sizes, see the table in <b>workflow 1 (Outfit Change)</b>: native 2K took about five times as long as 1 MP there, and it grows the same way here.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The graphics card peaked at about <b>19 GB</b> during these runs.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Writing the prompt</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Name each picture by its tag, <code>&lt;image1&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;image3&gt;</code>, and say what the person does with the object and where.</li><li>People and objects on a plain background are the easiest for the model to take from.</li><li><b>Say what must not change.</b> <code>Keep the room from &lt;image3&gt; exactly the same</code> keeps the whole room, so he sits in it at its own scale. For a closer photo, say how close the shot is instead, like <code>a medium shot from the waist up</code>.</li><li>Pick the shape of the new picture in step 4. To keep the room as it is, pick the room picture's shape: the demo room is square, so 1024 x 1024.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Tested on 8 seeds: every one kept his face, beard and black t-shirt, sat him in the wicker chair holding the mug with the logo to the camera, and kept the room. On 5 of them the room lines up with the room picture to within 2 pixels; on the other 3 the view moved a little.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The other edit workflows</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Kitchen attention, the memory node, the first Run of the session and the full size table are explained in <b>workflow 1 (Outfit Change)</b>. They work the same way here.</p>\", \"buttonColor\": \"#f66744\", \"lineColor\": \"#f66744\", \"width\": 810, \"height\": 767, \"backgroundColor\": \"#2a2a2a\"}",
